---
title: "I/O functions"
description: "Readers and writers, with their format-specific options."
---

## `read_csv` {#fn-read-csv}

```
tarn.read_csv(path, *, types=None, header=True, delimiter=",") -> Frame
```

Reads a delimited text file lazily. `types` overrides inferred column types by name;
see @sec-load-csv for when the inference goes wrong. With `header=False` the columns
are named `c0`, `c1`, … in order.

## `read_parquet` {#fn-read-parquet}

```
tarn.read_parquet(path, *, columns=None) -> Frame
```

Reads a Parquet file lazily, with the schema taken from the file. `columns` restricts
the read at the source; the planner also does this automatically from the query, so
pass it only when you want the restriction to be explicit.

## `write_csv` {#fn-write-csv}

```
Frame.write_csv(path, *, header=True) -> None
```

Collects the frame and writes it. This is a terminal operation: it runs the plan.

## `write_parquet` {#fn-write-parquet}

```
Frame.write_parquet(path, *, compression="zstd") -> None
```

Collects and writes, preserving the frame's schema so a later `read_parquet` round-trips
without inference.
